experiment: blockwhere
  instrument        blockwhere   trial seed 0000000001352ce7   2000 trials
                    another probe is another trial sequence: its numbers
                    are not comparable with these (~0.05 at 300 trials)
  question          `blockfloor` found one neuron of 14 costs 30% of the
                    lesson and four cost 57%. Is that about HOW MANY cells
                    are blocked, or about WHICH ONES?
  the two accounts  a faulty instrument, or LEVERAGE. `read_group` weights
                    neuron i by (i - begin + 0.5)/n, so index IS position,
                    and every block ever measured took the TOP of the group
                    -- the best levers for moving a weighted mean.
  the design        ONE neuron in every blocked arm, so the count is held
                    fixed and only its POSITION differs. Any difference is
                    leverage; no difference refutes it.
  the prediction    a weighted mean is least sensitive near its own centre,
                    so `mid1` should cost clearly less than `top1`. The two
                    ends need not match: the end the lesson travels TOWARD
                    should matter more.
  why it matters    `mask-unaffordable` closed write separation on "confining
                    a lesson is unaffordable". If the cost is leverage that
                    reads "unaffordable AT THE TOP", and separation bought in
                    the middle may be nearly free -- reopening a shut line.
  the anchor        `top1` must reproduce ~30%. If it does not, this run
                    disagrees with `blockfloor` and THAT is the finding.

  THE BLOCK AS BUILT (group is neurons 28..41 of vocal's 126)
    b0    nothing blocked
    top1  blocks index 41  (position 0.964 in the group)
    mid1  blocks index 34  (position 0.464 in the group)
    bot1  blocks index 28  (position 0.036 in the group)
    b0-475 nothing blocked
    top1-475 blocks index 41  (position 0.964 in the group)
    mid1-475 blocks index 34  (position 0.464 in the group)
    bot1-475 blocks index 28  (position 0.036 in the group)


  arm    err before   err taught   learned
  b0     1.0080       0.8404       +0.1676 +/- 0.0073
  top1   1.0183       0.9009       +0.1174 +/- 0.0071
  mid1   1.0048       0.8483       +0.1565 +/- 0.0083
  bot1   1.0182       0.8657       +0.1525 +/- 0.0076
  b0-475 0.6136       0.4525       +0.1610 +/- 0.0086
  top1-475 0.6224       0.5009       +0.1214 +/- 0.0068
  mid1-475 0.6102       0.4582       +0.1520 +/- 0.0082
  bot1-475 0.6227       0.4702       +0.1525 +/- 0.0082

  ARM LIVENESS vs `b0` (seeds where the arm differs at all)
    top1               36/36
    mid1               36/36
    bot1               36/36
    b0-475             36/36
    top1-475           36/36
    mid1-475           36/36
    bot1-475           36/36

  THE COST OF BLOCKING ONE NEURON, paired on seed against each arm's
  OWN unblocked control (named per arm; a single `b0` would charge the
  second-target arms the gap between the two conditions)
    top1      -0.0503 +/- 0.0086  (-5.8 SE)   30% of the lesson   (vs `b0`)
    mid1      -0.0112 +/- 0.0105  (-1.1 SE)   7% of the lesson   (vs `b0`)
    bot1      -0.0151 +/- 0.0105  (-1.4 SE)   9% of the lesson   (vs `b0`)
    top1-475  -0.0396 +/- 0.0094  (-4.2 SE)   25% of the lesson   (vs `b0-475`)
    mid1-475  -0.0091 +/- 0.0111  (-0.8 SE)   6% of the lesson   (vs `b0-475`)
    bot1-475  -0.0085 +/- 0.0115  (-0.7 SE)   5% of the lesson   (vs `b0-475`)

  DOES POSITION MATTER? paired on seed (positive = cheaper than `top1`)
    mid1 - top1  +0.0391 +/- 0.0108  (+3.6 SE)
    bot1 - top1  +0.0351 +/- 0.0106  (+3.3 SE)

  POSITION IS THE COST, NOT COUNT (3.6 SE). The same ONE neuron costs
  30% of the lesson at the top of the group and 7% in the middle.
  Nothing about the number blocked changed, so the instrument is exonerated
  -- `set_reward_block` does what it says -- and the readout's GEOMETRY is
  the finding: `read_group` weights neuron i by (i - begin + 0.5)/n, a
  weighted mean is least sensitive near its own centre, and every block
  this project ever measured took the most expensive cells available.

  THAT REOPENS WRITE SEPARATION. `mask-unaffordable` closed it on "confining
